course: dictionary
lesson: 12131
title: Commencement: the start, or the graduation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word commencement means a beginning or start. It is a formal word, so you will often see it in notices and letters. «The commencement of the lesson is at nine o'clock.» The clue is the time and the word lesson: something is about to begin.
explain: Look at «Before the commencement of the exam, the teacher read the rules.» The rules are read at the start of the exam, so commencement means start. Swap in start: «Before the start of the exam, the teacher read the rules» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: In the USA and Canada, the word can mean something different. «The students wore caps and gowns at the commencement ceremony.» Caps, gowns and a ceremony tell you it is a graduation. The same word can have two meanings, so the context tells you which one to choose.
fact: Commencement means the beginning or start of something.
fact: Commencement is a formal word, so you will see it in notices, letters and exam rules.
fact: In the USA and Canada, a commencement is a graduation ceremony, when students get their diplomas.
fact: «The commencement of the lesson» means the start of the lesson.
fact: A commencement speech is a talk given at a graduation ceremony.
exercise: «The commencement of the lesson was at nine o'clock.» What does commencement mean here? | A test | The end | A long break | *The start
exercise: In «Before the commencement of the exam, the teacher read the rules», what does commencement mean? | A cheat sheet | A break from the exam | The end of the exam | *The beginning of the exam
exercise: In the USA, what is a commencement? | *A graduation ceremony where students get their diplomas | A spelling test | A school bus | A type of lunch
test: «The students wore caps and gowns at the commencement ceremony.» What does commencement mean here? | A fire drill | *A graduation ceremony | A sports day | A lunch break
test: Which word is closest in meaning to commencement? | Mistake | *Start | Holiday | Ending
exam: Which sentence uses commencement to mean the start of something? | I washed my commencement | The commencement was a red bicycle | We played football in the commencement | *The commencement of the film was at seven o'clock
